Z||000002||86 FIERO GT||11-26-2001||07:33 PM||||Yes it does but it was originally red, and they painted it silver and did a really bad job, so id like to strip it and paint it.   The paint really looks good from a distance, but when you get up close you can see all the imperfections.<P>------------------<BR>86 Fiero GT , soon to be N*ed and worked over.||||reg||1
Z||000003||My7Fieros||11-26-2001||07:37 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by 86 FIERO GT:<BR><B>Yes it does but it was originally red, and they painted it silver and did a really bad job, so id like to strip it and paint it.   The paint really looks good from a distance, but when you get up close you can see all the imperfections.<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>It urks me to no end when someone paints a Fiero and are too lazy to take 2 minutes out of their time to take the damn body side molding off! Keep the molding black! Otherwise IMHO it just looks like a total (cheap) repaint. No offense to those of you who painted your moldings <I>on purpose</I>.<BR>I think torch red will look great, keep us posted!<P>||||reg||1
